*Subject: Application for Summer Intern 2026 – Nordea Markets (Risk & Quant Analytics / Trading Capital)*

Dear Hiring Team,

As a 1st year MSc student in Mathematical Modelling and Computation at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU), I am writing to express my strong interest in the 2026 Summer Internship program at Nordea Markets. With a background that merges rigorous mathematical analysis with software engineering and entrepreneurial initiative, I am eager to contribute to the largest trading floor in Scandinavia. I am particularly drawn to the *Risk & Quant Analytics* and *Trading Capital* teams, where I can apply my quantitative skills to complex, real-world financial challenges.

*Why Nordea?* \
Working in a start-up and a small consultancy learns you a lot about how take responsibility and critically find the most crucial tasks at hand, but I have in both occasions been missing the opportunity to learn from the best of the best in the industry. Therefore, I am excited by the prospect of learning from industry-leading quants and traders while contributing to the bank’s mission of enabling dreams through data-driven financial strategies.

*Quantitative Skills and Technical Insight* \
My academic journey at DTU has provided me with a robust foundation in applied mathematics and cyber systems. I have developed high proficiency in tools essential for modern finance, including *Python, SQL, F\#, Java, and Excel*. During my tenure at Nordic Marine Partner, I was responsible for developing an automated system to analyze and track technical performance. This required not only technical skill in Python but also the ability to translate complex datasets into actionable strategy reports.

*Software Development and Entrepreneurial Initiative* \
My entrepreneurial experience as a Co-founder of VetAlign has honed my ability to build complex systems from the ground up. I successfully developed a fully functional SaaS product using *C\# and NextJS*, which gave me deep insight into building reliable software architectures. Additionally, my technical toolkit includes experience with *F\#, Java, and Typescript*, as well as specialized knowledge in *Forecasting, Time Series Analysis, and Machine Learning* which was mainly done in Python. I thrive in environments where I can do sparring with colleagues to technical challenges and solve problems with a proactive, initiative-driven approach.

I am highly motivated to spend eight weeks of my summer learning from the experts at Nordea and contributing to your team's success. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my background in mathematical modelling and my proactive mindset can add value to Nordea Markets.

#v(1em)
Sincerely, \
